<title>ITALY: Alitalia loses appeal on Air One slots.</title>
<headline>Alitalia loses appeal on Air One slots.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Lazio adminstrative court said it rejected an appeal by Alitalia opposing the granting of a temporary licence to private sector carrier, Air One to carry passengers and cargo between Milan and Rome.</p>
<p>The licence was granted by Italy's Civil Aviation Authority last December, and allows Air One to use 14 slots on the route allocated to another small airline, Noman which has ceased activity. --Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44-171-542-7706 Fax+5017</p>
</text>
